# config/away-selfheal-command - the command the away-mode sub-supervisor types
# into the primary pane to bring the session back after it has verifiably exited
# (bin/fm-supervise-daemon.sh's selfheal_maybe). Copy this into a local,
# gitignored config/away-selfheal-command and edit. The FIRST non-empty,
# non-comment line is used; the rest is ignored.
#
# Self-healing is OFF while this file is absent and FM_AWAY_SELFHEAL_CMD is
# unset, so a home opts in deliberately rather than inheriting a restart.
#
# It must RESUME this home's session rather than start a fresh one: the daemon
# restarts the session shell to get delivery moving again, and everything the
# session was holding has to survive that. For Claude Code that is the --continue
# form; use whichever launcher and account this home actually runs.
#
#   claude --continue
#   claude3 --continue
#   codex resume --last
#
# The command is typed only AFTER the agent has been asked to leave through its
# own exit command and its stop has been confirmed, so it is always typed into a
# plain shell, never into an agent composer.
claude --continue
